A||N||13||Springtyme||Neon lights?||||1||
Z||000000||Springtyme||09-17-2001||12:54 PM||||Okay, okay, sue me, I want to rice out my car. Well, not really, but I want to deck it out. I want to put neon blue lights on the bottom, and change all the orange lights on the panels on the inside to blue also, like the new stereo I have... pics are below...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/my_stereo.JPG"> <BR>Stero during the day<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lights.JPG"> <BR>Setero during the night<P>How would I get all the other orange lights to be blue? Thanks for your help in advance!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Springtyme.jpg"> <P>            ~Springtyme~||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||09-17-2001||01:02 PM||||This would depend on what type of gages you have. If you have the backlit gages (120 mph speedo?), then you will need to get new gage overlays. AusFiero is working on them I believe. If you have frontlit gages, then you will need to remove the metal gage cover and paint it blue. Also, you will probably want to redo the idiot lights so that they light in blue. For the aux gages, they are all backlit, so you would need overlays for them (if you have aux gages).||||reg||1
Z||000002||falconhulk||09-17-2001||01:09 PM||||I just slapped some street glow neon blue fog lights on the front of my car and they rock!  They dont put out any useful illumanation but they look cool lit up.  They also look like 2 neon blue balls hanging in the front during the day when off.  They were a great addition for me.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Springtyme||09-17-2001||01:10 PM||||My speedo only goes to 85 (even though I wrapped the needle back around to 10, yes its a 4-banger... it was going downhill <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">) so what kind of paint would I use? Temer paint? also, where could I get it?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Springtyme.jpg"> <P>            ~Springtyme~||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||09-17-2001||01:28 PM||||springtyme-  Even though you have an '85mph speedo... it should be backlight.  Run a search for "indiglo" in the General section... there is a topic listed as "indiglo-look gauges" about some custom backlight gauges. (I've just got a prototype so far).<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000005||grinthock||09-17-2001||05:20 PM||||I work in a Car audio shop and we carry the complete line of Street Glow products, they are competition grade neon componants, as for the gauges if you get some EL paper you get do your own regardless of you having a 120 speedo or not.  See SlammedFIERO for details on that.<P>Neon stuff on the interior side can be mild OR wild, I am putting small neon accent lights in my interior, as well as in the intake.  The floor will light blue, the intake, and I have a custom dash kit going in with blue neon behind it.   We also have the HOT WIRES, which is like neon rope you can bend and flex as you like it.  Check out street glow's web site.  A complete unbody neon kit can be had for between $250-$500 Canadian dollars depending on where you buy it.  Prices are about the same in the states (beind more like $150-300 USD), that will get you a complete underbody kit of 2 4 foot and 2 3 foot tubes.  Keep in mind the underbody kit you use should be of the UTMOST quality.  As they take the most abuse beind exposed to the elements, and as always I do'nt reccomend using underbody kits in the winter or anytime when it's less than 32 deg F ( or 0 celcius)<P>As for the neon kit here is what I recently compelted.   Excuse the fuzz, it was a long exposure at night, handheld.  Apoligize about the pic size for dialup users.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fuzzyneon.JPG">  <P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif">  </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.<p>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 09-17-2001).]||||reg||1
